critical.issue:
Expression at server.py:326 'if expires_at and expires_at.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) if expires_at.tzinfo is None else expires_at < datetime.now(timezone.utc):' has wrong operator precedence. Python parses it as a ternary: `(expires_at and expires_at.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)) if (expires_at.tzinfo is None) else (expires_at < datetime.now(timezone.utc))`. PyMongo returns datetimes without tzinfo by default, so the ternary returns the new tz-aware datetime (truthy), causing the if-block to ALWAYS raise 400 'Token has expired'. Result: valid, non-expired reset tokens are rejected and admins can never reset their password via email link. Suggested fix: replace with explicit two-line normalisation:
    if expires_at.tzinfo is None:
        expires_at = expires_at.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)
    if expires_at < datetime.now(timezone.utc):
        raise HTTPException(400, 'Token has expired')
